 "url": "https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2022/02/grammar-of-good-leader.html",
 "selfLink": "https://www.googleapis.com/blogger/v3/blogs/6417357851361576411/posts/3366344962027579206",
 "title": "Grammar of good leader.",
 "content": "<p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p><h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #274e13;\"><span style=\"font-size: large;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Grammar of good leader.</span></span></span></h2><h2><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></h2><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Be a cooperative person.</span></span></h3><h3><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></h3><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">One would not \nbe a good leader without been cooperative with team members. There is a \npopular story from the history of America. Once there were four men \ntrying to lift a wood in forest area, the orders was given by the \nsupervisor on how to lift the tree, but that four men thought it would \nbe easier to lift that wood if they have another person to help, but the\n supervisor not ready to help them. One that way one man was come in a \nhorse and help that men to lift the wood and ask the supervisor why he \nwas not ready to help the workers, supervisor said he is lead for the \nworkers, and it is not his job to work with them other than give orders.\n Rider in the horse similes and replied “I am George Washington \", I am \nsuperior to all of you and also ready to work with you, rather than not \njust give the orders”. Supervisor astonished for a second and felt sorry\n for his attitude.<br />So, the above story teaches us how to be a cooperative person in workspace.</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"></span></p><div class=\"separator\" style=\"clear: both; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEiMP0WxpYZeHLs4oHTmhWuhml3a_d7FwZ6rFs9U87Wd0ZhRpIfI7Sn3Zbxmvf-Z9ARQEGs0hjSN70C1_N7p3FqowaNU4fYCPMfEHJ0ikEFd4_Fi5YBClJotvA1Wa9_D5UYcUL3I3QqZHq8JbITopGoH-7oYKVNRC455mL8rteVDpsDOGJS1YCGGm3DmAA=s6016\" imageanchor=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;\"><img border=\"0\" data-original-height=\"4000\" data-original-width=\"6016\" height=\"213\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEiMP0WxpYZeHLs4oHTmhWuhml3a_d7FwZ6rFs9U87Wd0ZhRpIfI7Sn3Zbxmvf-Z9ARQEGs0hjSN70C1_N7p3FqowaNU4fYCPMfEHJ0ikEFd4_Fi5YBClJotvA1Wa9_D5UYcUL3I3QqZHq8JbITopGoH-7oYKVNRC455mL8rteVDpsDOGJS1YCGGm3DmAA=s320\" width=\"320\" /></a></span></div><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><br /><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"><br /></span></span><p></p><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Set goals.</span></span></h3><h3><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></h3><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">One\n wouldn’t be a leader without know about the goals. Good leader should \nknow about his/her next step and have proper understanding about their \nabilities. There should be proper planning to achieve the goals. A \nleader should not be stick around in a stand still situation. He must \nhave the courage to move forward in any circumstances.</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"></span></p><div class=\"separator\" style=\"clear: both; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEhpbvXGhEMdtQf3E8grzHetMgKM2cCUzE_XG3pLK5xYJGFa_Y_0T7DzV2G0YcEuN2Kv9j1cQA04aGxxxQAFI1PMnwiylWZUHJP2N_R3OKcRt17ud1Ix0ptQRB5H7e-tnVMd_xx7WVITunctmnf7Yh3IthaxXzBgTNIHW0KYjay6yLZSNHj7xPyqv1h-BQ=s6000\" imageanchor=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;\"><img border=\"0\" data-original-height=\"4004\" data-original-width=\"6000\" height=\"214\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEhpbvXGhEMdtQf3E8grzHetMgKM2cCUzE_XG3pLK5xYJGFa_Y_0T7DzV2G0YcEuN2Kv9j1cQA04aGxxxQAFI1PMnwiylWZUHJP2N_R3OKcRt17ud1Ix0ptQRB5H7e-tnVMd_xx7WVITunctmnf7Yh3IthaxXzBgTNIHW0KYjay6yLZSNHj7xPyqv1h-BQ=s320\" width=\"320\" /></a></span></div><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><br /><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span><br /><p></p><h4 style=\"text-align: left;\"><i><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: times;\"><i><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"color: #04ff00;\"><span style=\"color: #2b00fe;\"><u><b><span style=\"font-family: times;\">please disable adblocker and allow us to show some advertisements.</span></b></u></span></span></span></i></span></span></i></h4><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></p><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Responsibility</span></span></h3><h3><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></h3><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Don’t\n criticize others if something goes wrong in your team, handle the \nsituation and help your team to step out from that problem. You should \nnot say it's not your mistake if someone in your team does that. A good \nleader doesn’t run away or deserted their team members in unfortunate \nevent, he should be the first one who have to face the situation and own\n the responsibility.</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></p><div class=\"separator\" style=\"clear: both; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEi0tKZCNi18g9zjgPc132x-FAqqnw2rt3SoIZ3XcPADW9VFph_m-yqjrh-hlw2oxDM3W_HUELkLMVKrYnNh8hpPKzjD8aQrG2gLiymPRekDZJDXI3KvmyXdK0ICeNxWK0LY0IHl_DR0Vh2CY3LsTPRrKx22A0bl1aH_0-JwTD9xyhO8KFWfKmjhE_fJ7g=s5000\" imageanchor=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;\"><img border=\"0\" data-original-height=\"3337\" data-original-width=\"5000\" height=\"214\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEi0tKZCNi18g9zjgPc132x-FAqqnw2rt3SoIZ3XcPADW9VFph_m-yqjrh-hlw2oxDM3W_HUELkLMVKrYnNh8hpPKzjD8aQrG2gLiymPRekDZJDXI3KvmyXdK0ICeNxWK0LY0IHl_DR0Vh2CY3LsTPRrKx22A0bl1aH_0-JwTD9xyhO8KFWfKmjhE_fJ7g=s320\" width=\"320\" /></a></span></div><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><br />&nbsp;</span><p></p><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2021/12/the-mental-toughness-guide-how-to.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"><b>The Mental Toughness Guide: How to Develop Unbreakable Inner Strength!!!. </b></span></a><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"><b>🤔</b></span></span><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></p><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Share the victory.</span></span></h3><h3><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></h3><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">It is important that a \nleader should share the victory with team members. He should not think \nthat he is the only responsibility for the success. There are so many \nfactors needs to form a success.</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"></span></p><div class=\"separator\" style=\"clear: both; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEisHMR3t9AXCgVm9eGUE2o98Xp7cysYQ-0x_oXbR-di8ZCxEOwNLhhEJtEntL1IJPhMf0iw1ZCftSUnffzfAHBcKeQgHqdxLB-jD68zhGx96Ku23tq6QsKnNO2_OKGA5YfRrMqbJzRFIYboC-Etq5H4-ivaIVhddj6nOa84pUz8Ad8u7zNXBdhXas385g=s4176\" imageanchor=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;\"><img border=\"0\" data-original-height=\"2784\" data-original-width=\"4176\" height=\"213\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEisHMR3t9AXCgVm9eGUE2o98Xp7cysYQ-0x_oXbR-di8ZCxEOwNLhhEJtEntL1IJPhMf0iw1ZCftSUnffzfAHBcKeQgHqdxLB-jD68zhGx96Ku23tq6QsKnNO2_OKGA5YfRrMqbJzRFIYboC-Etq5H4-ivaIVhddj6nOa84pUz8Ad8u7zNXBdhXas385g=s320\" width=\"320\" /></a></span></div><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><br /><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"><br /></span></span><p></p><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Gather strength.</span></span></h3><h3><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Form a team of \nstrong minds and ask their options and ideas to handle the situations. \nSolo man can’t able to achieve huge success. Gather team of skillful \npersons and work with them to achieve the goals.</span></span></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"></span></p><div class=\"separator\" style=\"clear: both; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEipiRdlLCFPtg8to-hXwdtHSr4mCfUj2kpUuPe75KvSu7s8GA2XQhDlBQb8Af5IIlfzgfdhZQRmzq6okR_CMy6ogm1G7muU9MzhfV3W5TWihcLl6Je53I8L9Q3U5pBFooXxptb4MZMcYLMfw2FiO_NiQT9SKohWcaWJKn9Ih58xsaBpFFX8I-NFJY_bYw=s4936\" imageanchor=\"1\" style=\"margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;\"><img border=\"0\" data-original-height=\"3291\" data-original-width=\"4936\" height=\"213\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEipiRdlLCFPtg8to-hXwdtHSr4mCfUj2kpUuPe75KvSu7s8GA2XQhDlBQb8Af5IIlfzgfdhZQRmzq6okR_CMy6ogm1G7muU9MzhfV3W5TWihcLl6Je53I8L9Q3U5pBFooXxptb4MZMcYLMfw2FiO_NiQT9SKohWcaWJKn9Ih58xsaBpFFX8I-NFJY_bYw=s320\" width=\"320\" /></a></span></div><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><br /><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"><br /></span></span><p></p><h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: red;\"><u><i><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: times;\"><span style=\"font-size: large;\"><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/2021/07/why-indians-are-too-religious.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #351c75;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Religion in India..?🤔click here!!!</span></span></span></a></span></span></span></i></u></span></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></p><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Confidence</span></span></h3><h3><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\"></span></span></h3><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Self confidence is the key for the leadership. You can’t motivate others if you have not the courage to move forward.</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p><h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://randomthoughtsever.blogspot.com/p/trending-posts_53.html\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #351c75;\"><u><i><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">Trending posts..😲😵click here!!!</span></span></i></u></span></a></h3><p><span style=\"font-family: times;\"><br /></span></p><div><p><span style=\"font-family: times;\"><i><span><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><u><span><i><span style=\"color: red;\"><b><span style=\"font-size: large;\"><span>Thanks for reading this blog,please share with others and help us to grow<span style=\"font-size: medium;\">.</span></span></span></b></span></i></span></u></span></span></i><i><span><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><br /><br /><span style=\"color: red;\"><u><b><br /></b></u></span></span></span></i></span></p><h2><span style=\"font-family: times;\"><span style=\"font-size: large;\"><i><span><span><span style=\"color: red;\"><u><b>Please visit this blog again!!!we uploads articles daily!!!!😀😀</b></u></span></span></span></i></span></span></h2></div><p><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"font-family: georgia;\">&nbsp;</span></span></p>",
